{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc && sed -n '135,190p' src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc && rg -n 'dyn|scope' test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the PHP tests (P6, docs/design/\n   yang.php.md section 11): the namespace that requires this is the\n   publisher of `php`, so it publishes the module once per process into one\n   in-memory content store, publishes a fixture's non-entry units beside it\n   bottom-up, and serves them to the entry unit's run over a\n   `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under `:trusted` derivation.\n\n   A linked run builds the entry unit's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately until\n   the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker is not a\n   backend here: its link of `php` is refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.php.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yang.safepoint :as sp]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The host registry a linked PHP composition registers: the `require`\n   handlers, then `cell`, `data` and `integer` under the portable limits.\"\n  []\n  (portable/linked-registry))\n\n\n(defn make-published\n  \"Create a store with the linked runtime and its hook module.\"\n  []\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n        result (publish/publish-module! store (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                                   (:address call-result)))\n        hook (publish/publish-module! store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) (:address result)))]\n    {:store store,\n     :hook-address (:address hook),\n     :result result,\n     :address (:address result),\n     :call-address (:address call-result)}))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `php` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay (make-published)))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"`units` (`[{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}]`) published into\n   `php`'s own content store, where its pinned requirement already lives:\n   `publication/publish-units!`'s answer.\"\n  [units]\n  (publication/publish-units! (:store @published) (registry) (:address @published) units))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The linked store and signed site publications for this fixture.\"\n  ([name-env] (source name-env nil))\n  ([name-env result]\n   (let [publisher (sign/generate)\n         entries (siteset/signed-entries publisher (:sites result)\n                                         (:addresses result) (:bundles result))\n         datoms (siteset/entry-datoms entries)\n         stage (siteset/stage (registry)\n                              {:hooks true, :hooks-profile safepoint/ticks-profile,\n                               :php-sp (:hook-address @published)} {})]\n     (link/composition\n       {:content-store (:store @published),\n        :name-env (merge {'php (:address @published),\n                          'php.sp (:hook-address @published),\n                          'yang.call (:call-address @published)} name-env),\n        :derivation :trusted,\n        :stage (fn [ctx name address]\n                 (stage (assoc ctx :datoms datoms :principals [(:public publisher)])\n                        name address))}))))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task stops\n   blocking, at most 80 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 80))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`, served from\n   `src`. A refused link surfaces as the program's own diagnostics.\"\n  [backend ast src]\n  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n        task ((get backends backend) ast (composition (registry) pair))]\n    (first (drive task pair src))))\n\n\n(defn name-env\n  \"The name environment naming every published module of `result`\n   (`publish-units!`'s answer): module symbol to address.\"\n  [result]\n  (merge (into {} (map (fn [[path address]] [(lower/path-module-symbol path) address]))\n               (:addresses result))\n         (:bundles result)))\n\n\n(defn run-fixture\n  \"`{backend value}` for the multi-unit fixture `units` (`{path packet}`,\n   the entry unit `main`, default `lower/entry-path`) on the three vector\n   VMs: the non-entry units are published bottom-up, the entry unit\n   lowered `:linked` and run. `value` is `run-main`'s map.\"\n  ([units] (run-fixture units lower/entry-path {}))\n  ([units main opts]\n   (let [entry (get units main)\n         others (cond-> (mapv (fn [[path packet]] {:name path, :packet packet})\n                              (dissoc units main))\n                  (:class-map opts) (conj (assoc (:class-map opts) :name lower/classmap-name)))\n         result (publish-units! others)]\n     (when-not (= :ok (:status result))\n       (throw (ex-info \"fixture units failed to publish\" {:result result})))\n     (let [{:keys [ast warnings]}\n           (lower/lower-program entry\n                                (cond-> (merge {:prelude :linked,\n                                                :path main,\n                                                :paths (when (:computed? opts) (keys (:addresses result)))}\n                                               (dissoc opts :computed? :src :request))\n                                  (:class-map opts) (assoc :class-map true)\n                                  (some? (:request opts)) (assoc :request-node\n                                                                 (portable/request-node (:request opts)))))\n           src (or (:src opts) (source (name-env result) result))\n           sites (:set (siteset/site-set-of ast))\n           tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n           ast (u/seq-nodes [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)\n                             (core-module/require-node 'php)\n                             (core-module/require-node 'php.sp)\n                             (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n\n\n(defn closure\n  \"Mint a closure owned by `owner` over the kernel payload map `payload`.\n   A trusted constructor: only kernels call it, never a guest primitive.\"\n  [owner payload]\n  (Closure. owner payload))\n\n\n(defn continuation\n  \"Mint a captured continuation owned by `owner` over the kernel payload\n   map `payload`. A trusted constructor, as `closure`.\"\n  [owner payload]\n  (Continuation. owner payload))\n\n\n(defn closure?\n  \"True when `x` is a closure a kernel minted. A type test: no map is a\n   closure, whatever keys it carries.\"\n  [x]\n  (instance? Closure x))\n\n\n(defn continuation?\n  \"True when `x` is a continuation a kernel captured. A type test.\"\n  [x]\n  (instance? Continuation x))\n\n\n(defn host-typed?\n  \"True when `x` is a closure or a continuation.\"\n  [x]\n  (or (closure? x) (continuation? x)))\n\n\n(defn payload\n  \"The kernel payload map of closure or continuation `x`.\"\n  [x]\n  (if (closure? x)\n    (.-payload ^Closure x)\n    (.-payload ^Continuation x)))\n\n\n(defn owner\n  \"The owner tag of closure or continuation `x`.\"\n  [x]\n  (if (closure? x)\n    (.-owner ^Closure x)\n    (.-owner ^Continuation x)))\n\n\n(defn owned-by?\n  \"True when closure or continuation `x` was minted by the task whose\n   owner tag is `tag`.\"\n  [x tag]\n  (let [o (owner x)]\nrg: test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
